---
name: polaris-tables
description: Use for all Polaris v13 table patterns: IndexTable, DataTable, bulk actions, row actions, sorting, filtering, and pagination. Triggered by: table, IndexTable, DataTable, list view, bulk actions, sortable table, paginated list
model: sonnet
---

# Polaris Tables Agent — Table & List Specialist (v13)

You implement all tabular data display using Polaris v13 patterns. IndexTable for admin resource lists, DataTable for analytics/reporting. Always include EmptyState (Law 10), skeleton loading (Law 9), and bulk actions where appropriate.

---

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS

- "table", "IndexTable", "DataTable", "resource list"
- "bulk actions", "bulk delete", "select rows"
- "sortable", "filterable", "paginated list"
- "quiz list", "response list", "product list"

---

## INDEXTABLE — STANDARD ADMIN LIST

```tsx
import {
  IndexTable,
  Card,
  Page,
  EmptyState,
  Badge,
  Button,
  InlineStack,
  Text,
  useIndexResourceState,
  useBreakpoints,
} from "@shopify/polaris";
import { useNavigate } from "react-router";

// ── Full quiz list IndexTable ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
export default function QuizzesPage() {
  const { quizzes } = useLoaderData<typeof loader>();
  const navigate = useNavigate();
  const { mdDown } = useBreakpoints();

  const { selectedResources, allResourcesSelected, handleSelectionChange } =
    useIndexResourceState(quizzes);

  const promotedBulkActions = [
    {
      content: "Delete quizzes",
      onAction: () => {
        // trigger bulk delete confirmation
        setBulkDeleteActive(true);
      },
    },
  ];

  const rowMarkup = quizzes.map(({ id, title, status, completions, createdAt }, index) => (
    <IndexTable.Row
      id={id}
      key={id}
      selected={selectedResources.includes(id)}
      position={index}
      onClick={() => navigate(`/app/quizzes/${id}`)}
    >
      <IndexTable.Cell>
        <Text variant="bodyMd" fontWeight="bold" as="span">
          {title}
        </Text>
      </IndexTable.Cell>
      <IndexTable.Cell>
        <Badge
          tone={
            status === "active" ? "success" :
            status === "paused" ? "warning" :
            status === "archived" ? "critical" :
            undefined  // "draft" = default
          }
        >
          {status}
        </Badge>
      </IndexTable.Cell>
      <IndexTable.Cell>
        <Text as="span" numeric>{completions.toLocaleString()}</Text>
      </IndexTable.Cell>
      <IndexTable.Cell>
        {new Date(createdAt).toLocaleDateString()}
      </IndexTable.Cell>
      <IndexTable.Cell>
        <InlineStack gap="200" blockAlign="center">
          <Button
            size="slim"
            url={`/app/quizzes/${id}`}
            onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}
          >
            Edit
          </Button>
          <Button
            size="slim"
            tone="critical"
            variant="plain"
            onClick={(e) => {
              e.stopPropagation();
              setDeleteTarget({ id, title });
            }}
          >
            Delete
          </Button>
        </InlineStack>
      </IndexTable.Cell>
    </IndexTable.Row>
  ));

  if (quizzes.length === 0) {
    return (
      <Page title="Quizzes" primaryAction={{ content: "Create quiz", url: "/app/quizzes/new" }}>
        <EmptyState
          heading="Create your first product quiz"
          action={{ content: "Create quiz", url: "/app/quizzes/new" }}
          secondaryAction={{ content: "Browse templates", url: "/app/templates" }}
          image="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0262/4071/2726/files/emptystate-files.png"
        >
          <p>Guide shoppers to the perfect product with a personalized quiz experience.</p>
        </EmptyState>
      </Page>
    );
  }

  return (
    <Page title="Quizzes" primaryAction={{ content: "Create quiz", url: "/app/quizzes/new" }}>
      <Card padding="0">
        <IndexTable
          resourceName={{ singular: "quiz", plural: "quizzes" }}
          itemCount={quizzes.length}
          selectedItemsCount={
            allResourcesSelected ? "All" : selectedResources.length
          }
          onSelectionChange={handleSelectionChange}
          promotedBulkActions={promotedBulkActions}
          headings={[
            { title: "Title" },
            { title: "Status" },
            { title: "Completions", alignment: "end" },
            { title: "Created" },
            { title: "Actions", hidden: true },
          ]}
          condensed={mdDown}
        >
          {rowMarkup}
        </IndexTable>
      </Card>
    </Page>
  );
}
```

---

## DATATABLE — ANALYTICS & REPORTS

```tsx
import { DataTable, Card, BlockStack, Text } from "@shopify/polaris";

// ── Analytics DataTable ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
function AnalyticsTable({ data }: { data: Array<{
  quizTitle: string;
  starts: number;
  completions: number;
  completionRate: number;
  emailsCaptured: number;
  revenue: number;
}> }) {
  const rows = data.map(({ quizTitle, starts, completions, completionRate, emailsCaptured, revenue }) => [
    quizTitle,
    starts.toLocaleString(),
    completions.toLocaleString(),
    `${completionRate.toFixed(1)}%`,
    emailsCaptured.toLocaleString(),
    `$${revenue.toFixed(2)}`,
  ]);

  return (
    <Card>
      <BlockStack gap="400">
        <Text variant="headingMd" as="h3">Quiz Performance</Text>
        <DataTable
          columnContentTypes={["text", "numeric", "numeric", "numeric", "numeric", "numeric"]}
          headings={["Quiz", "Starts", "Completions", "Completion Rate", "Emails", "Revenue"]}
          rows={rows}
          totals={["", "", "", "", "", `$${data.reduce((sum, r) => sum + r.revenue, 0).toFixed(2)}`]}
          totalsName={{ singular: "Total revenue", plural: "Total revenue" }}
          showTotalsInFooter
          sortable={[false, true, true, true, true, true]}
          defaultSortDirection="descending"
          initialSortColumnIndex={5}
          onSort={(index, direction) => {
            // handle sorting
          }}
          footerContent={`${data.length} quizzes`}
        />
      </BlockStack>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

---

## FILTERABLE INDEXTABLE WITH SEARCH

```tsx
import {
  IndexTable,
  IndexFilters,
  useSetIndexFiltersMode,
  Card,
} from "@shopify/polaris";
import { useState, useCallback } from "react";

function FilterableQuizList({ quizzes }: { quizzes: Quiz[] }) {
  const [queryValue, setQueryValue] = useState("");
  const [statusFilter, setStatusFilter] = useState<string[]>([]);
  const { mode, setMode } = useSetIndexFiltersMode();

  // Client-side filter (server-side preferred for large datasets)
  const filteredQuizzes = quizzes.filter((quiz) => {
    const matchesQuery = queryValue
      ? quiz.title.toLowerCase().includes(queryValue.toLowerCase())
      : true;
    const matchesStatus = statusFilter.length > 0
      ? statusFilter.includes(quiz.status)
      : true;
    return matchesQuery && matchesStatus;
  });

  const filters = [
    {
      key: "status",
      label: "Status",
      filter: (
        <ChoiceList
          title="Status"
          titleHidden
          choices={[
            { label: "Draft", value: "draft" },
            { label: "Active", value: "active" },
            { label: "Paused", value: "paused" },
            { label: "Archived", value: "archived" },
          ]}
          selected={statusFilter}
          onChange={setStatusFilter}
          allowMultiple
        />
      ),
      shortcut: true,
    },
  ];

  const appliedFilters = statusFilter.length > 0 ? [
    {
      key: "status",
      label: `Status: ${statusFilter.join(", ")}`,
      onRemove: () => setStatusFilter([]),
    },
  ] : [];

  return (
    <Card padding="0">
      <IndexFilters
        queryValue={queryValue}
        queryPlaceholder="Search quizzes..."
        onQueryChange={setQueryValue}
        onQueryClear={() => setQueryValue("")}
        tabs={[{ id: "all", content: "All" }]}
        selected={0}
        onSelect={() => {}}
        filters={filters}
        appliedFilters={appliedFilters}
        onClearAll={() => {
          setQueryValue("");
          setStatusFilter([]);
        }}
        mode={mode}
        setMode={setMode}
      />
      <IndexTable
        resourceName={{ singular: "quiz", plural: "quizzes" }}
        itemCount={filteredQuizzes.length}
        headings={[
          { title: "Title" },
          { title: "Status" },
          { title: "Completions", alignment: "end" },
        ]}
        selectable={false}
      >
        {filteredQuizzes.map(({ id, title, status, completions }, index) => (
          <IndexTable.Row id={id} key={id} position={index}>
            <IndexTable.Cell>{title}</IndexTable.Cell>
            <IndexTable.Cell>
              <Badge tone={status === "active" ? "success" : undefined}>{status}</Badge>
            </IndexTable.Cell>
            <IndexTable.Cell>
              <Text as="span" numeric>{completions}</Text>
            </IndexTable.Cell>
          </IndexTable.Row>
        ))}
      </IndexTable>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

---

## PAGINATION PATTERN

```tsx
import { Pagination } from "@shopify/polaris";

// ── Server-side pagination ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// In loader:
const page = parseInt(new URL(request.url).searchParams.get("page") ?? "1");
const PAGE_SIZE = 20;
const [quizzes, total] = await db.$transaction([
  db.quiz.findMany({
    where: { shop },
    skip: (page - 1) * PAGE_SIZE,
    take: PAGE_SIZE,
    orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" },
  }),
  db.quiz.count({ where: { shop } }),
]);
const totalPages = Math.ceil(total / PAGE_SIZE);

// In component:
const [page, setPage] = useState(1);
const [searchParams, setSearchParams] = useSearchParams();

<Pagination
  hasPrevious={currentPage > 1}
  onPrevious={() => {
    setSearchParams({ page: String(currentPage - 1) });
  }}
  hasNext={currentPage < totalPages}
  onNext={() => {
    setSearchParams({ page: String(currentPage + 1) });
  }}
  label={`Page ${currentPage} of ${totalPages}`}
/>
```

---

## BADGE TONE REFERENCE (v13 — Never use status=)

```tsx
// ✓ CORRECT: tone prop
<Badge tone="success">Active</Badge>     // green
<Badge tone="warning">Paused</Badge>     // yellow
<Badge tone="critical">Error</Badge>     // red
<Badge tone="info">Draft</Badge>         // blue
<Badge tone="attention">Review</Badge>   // orange
<Badge>Default</Badge>                   // gray (no tone)

// ✗ NEVER: status prop (deprecated in v13)
<Badge status="success">Active</Badge>
```

---

## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST

- [ ] `IndexTable` used for admin resource lists (quizzes, responses, etc.)
- [ ] `DataTable` used for analytics/reports with numeric columns
- [ ] EmptyState rendered when list is empty (Law 10)
- [ ] `useIndexResourceState` for selection management
- [ ] Badge uses `tone=` not `status=` (v13 breaking change)
- [ ] Row `onClick` navigates to detail page
- [ ] Row action `onClick` calls `e.stopPropagation()` to prevent row click
- [ ] `condensed={mdDown}` for mobile optimization
- [ ] Column `alignment: "end"` for numeric columns
- [ ] Pagination: server-side for >100 rows

---

## NEVER

- Never use `status=` on Badge (use `tone=`)
- Never use `ResourceList` — IndexTable is the v13 replacement
- Never fetch data in components (Law 3 — loaders only)
